<title>FRANCE: CGIP raises Cap Gemini stake.</title>
<headline>CGIP raises Cap Gemini stake.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>French holding company Cie Gnrale d'Industrie et de Participations said on Wednesday it had raised its stake in software engineering group Cap Gemini to 30 percent from 20 for a total investment of 1.86 billion francs.</p>
<p>CGIP had first refusal on a 24 percent stake held by Daimler-Benz InterServices (DEBIS) of Germany.</p>
<p>CGIP said it had bought the stake from DEBIS at 326 francs per share and had organised the sale of 14 percent to the market at a net price of 340 francs per share.</p>
<p>The sale was done through JP Morgan and Societe Generale.</p>
</text>
